[medium] internal/service/relational/suggestions/core.go:159 (correctness)
canonicalLabelLines lowercases keys for sorting but then looks the value back up by ranging the original labels map. A label map containing case variants such as Env=prod and env=stage can pick either value depending on Go map iteration order, and it emits duplicate lowercased lines. That makes label_set_hash nondeterministic for valid evidence_labels rows that differ only by key case, and accepted filters built from those labels may not be re-detected by CanonicalizeFilter because conflicting duplicate conditions are rejected.
Suggested fix: Normalize label maps to a single lowercased key before hashing/building filters. Reject or skip label sets with conflicting case-folded duplicate keys, and collapse same-value duplicates deterministically. Cover CanonicalLabelSetHash and gatherAllLabelSets with case-variant label tests.
Guidance: Fix internal/service/relational/suggestions/core.go and the evidence-label gather path. Add a helper such as NormalizeLabelSet(labels map[string]string) (map[string]string, bool) that lowercases keys, preserves values exactly, collapses duplicate case-folded keys only when the values are identical, and returns ok=false when the same lowercased key has different values. Refactor canonicalLabelLines to operate on an already-normalized map with sorted keys and no nested scan over the original map. Keep CanonicalLabelSetHash(labels map[string]string) string for existing filter-derived and test callers by normalizing internally; for conflicting duplicates it must still be deterministic, so use the normalized value only when ok=true and otherwise hash a sorted representation that includes every original lowercased key/value pair rather than picking the first map iteration value. In internal/service/relational/suggestions/gather.go gatherAllLabelSets, call NormalizeLabelSet on group.labels before hashing/copying; if ok=false, skip that evidence's label set entirely so model-visible label_set_hashes are never based on contradictory case-folded duplicates. When ok=true, store the normalized labels in LabelSetInput so later fallbackFilterName, validation, and accept BuildLabelFilter receive lowercase keys and exact original values. Do not lowercase values, do not accept OR/!= filters, and do not change global filter behavior. Add tests in internal/service/relational/suggestions/core_test.go for same-value case duplicates collapsing and conflicting case duplicates producing deterministic distinct hashes, plus a gatherAllLabelSets test showing conflicting evidence labels are skipped and same-value case duplicates produce one normalized label hash.

